  "Number": 16,
  "Question": "Joyce made \\(12\\) of her first \\(30\\) shots in the first three games of the basketball season, so her seasonal shooting average was \\(40\\%.\\) In her next game, she took \\(10\\) shots and raised her seasonal shooting average to \\(50\\%.\\) How many of these \\(10\\) shots did she make?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(3\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The new seasonal percentage applies to all of Joyce's shots so far. After the next game, she had taken\n\\[\n30+10=40\\text{ shots}.\n\\]\nSince \\(50\\%\\) means one half, she had made \\(40\\div2=20\\) shots altogether. She had already made \\(12\\) before that game, so the number she made in the new game was\n\\[\n20-12=8.\n\\]\nThus she made \\(8\\) of those shots, choice E.",
